      "dialog": {
        "start": "open",
        "nodes": {
          "open": {
            "branch": [
              {
                "when": {
                  "flag": "met"
                },
                "to": "again"
              },
              {
                "to": "hello"
              }
            ]
          },
          "hello": {
            "text": [
              "Boots. Either sand or sheep, and I would rather guess than know.",
              "Ivy. I sell to the boats and I sell to the hill, and neither lot will admit the other keeps me open."
            ],
            "do": {
              "set": "met"
            },
            "then": "menu"
          },
          "again": {
            "text": "Back down, or back up? What is it?",
            "then": "menu"
          },
          "menu": {
            "text": "Trading, or sheltering?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Trading.",
                "do": {
                  "shop": true
                },
                "to": "after"
              },
              {
                "text": "What'll you take?",
                "to": "takes"
              },
              {
                "text": "Sheltering.",
                "to": "bye"
              }
            ]
          },
          "takes": {
            "text": "Shells, stone, wood, flowers. Doss will beat me on shells and he will tell you so himself.",
            "then": "menu"
          },
          "after": {
            "text": "Right you are.",
            "then": "menu"
          },
          "bye": {
            "text": "Pull it to. The wind takes it."
          }
        },
        "greetings": {
          "acquaintance": [
            "Boat lot were in first, so the rope is gone. Hill lot will be in for the feed. You are neither, which is restful.",
            "Kelp wants rope, Nell wants feed, and both of them want it cheaper. Chandlery and feed. It is on the sign.",
            "Sand on the floor from one side and mud from the other. I sweep it into a pile and call it Bellrock.",
            "Every time Morrow tests a bell, the shop empties. I have not decided whether it is the noise or the omen."
          ],
          "friend": [
            "Doss told you he pays more for shells. He does. He also pays in Doss, which is a currency of opinions.",
            "Sennen came in to stand in the middle of the shop. I think it is a habit now, not a position.",
            "You have been up the hill and down to the boats in the same pair of boots. That makes you the only one in town who has.",
            "Chalk asked if I had a wall going spare. Told him the wind already took the paint off the last one."
          ],
          "close": [
            "Lean on the counter. It is the one thing in here the wind has not moved.",
            "I saved you the last of the cress seed before the hill lot got at it.",
            "Door held itself shut this once. I am putting it down to you."
          ]
        }
      }
    }
